      "postID": "5c94de45f293525fe7ad1432",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think that the performance impact of avatars on new players with dynamic bone counts exceeding 32 bones in a full room would be more important. If a new player notices anything peculiar they usually ask, this is the case with personal space and with the comfort turning. It would be better for people to see the performance change as a new player first and allow them to choose to leave the limiter off and see the high dynamic bone count at the cost of performance than that would be user preference rather than having some leave the game due to the performance drop others cause or learning about the limiter a few months after starting and wishing they knew about it sooner. (Side note: some of this is paraphrased from what someone else said, I just agree with their view on the limiter defaulting on.)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
